= The Free Unions and Staal

Tobias Leighart and the ADGB's vice chairmen have requested a meeting with Chancellor von Staal to discuss the funding of Staal's planned public works program, which Gereke has almost finished despite Staal unwilling to cut through red tape to speed up the process for him. 

However, Staal has used this meeting to discuss the possibility of the ADGB endorsing his planned postponement of new elections, which the organization denounced any potential breach of the constitution. [? if heartland_leader == "Staal": "Anti-Staal sentiment has grown so much in the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> parties, that Lyle Bristol reversed his earlier willingness to join with the chancellor in asking the president to postpone elections unconstitutionally. ?]

However, the obsession of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> to prevent a breach of the constitution by Staal or Goodryke at all costs has caused many leaders, with the possible exception of Bristol, to lose sight of the real peril: [+ royalist_chancellor +]'s appointment to the chancellorship.

- @root: Need not to worry, after all, DuFour will never appoint [+ royalist_chancellor +]!